       EEIINNVVAALL _a_d_d_r  is not a multiple of the system page size or _s_i_z_e is nega‐
              tive.

       EEIINNVVAALL _a_d_v_i_c_e is invalid.

       EENNOOMMEEMM Addresses in the specified range  are  partially  or  completely
              outside the caller’s address space.

VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       POSIX.1  permits  an  implementation to generate an error if _s_i_z_e is 0.
       On Linux, specifying _s_i_z_e as 0 is permitted (as a successful no‐op).

       In glibc, this function  is  implemented  using  mmaaddvviissee(2).   However,
       since glibc 2.6, PPOOSSIIXX__MMAADDVV__DDOONNTTNNEEEEDD is treated as a no‐op, because the
       corresponding  mmaaddvviissee(2)  value, MMAADDVV__DDOONNTTNNEEEEDD, has destructive seman‐
       tics.

